<title>MEXICO: Banco de Mexico completes secondary participation.</title>
<headline>Banco de Mexico completes secondary participation.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico has assigned all three direct sales of paper and the three repurchase agreements whereby it had sought to drain 1.591 billion pesos from the secondary market on Tuesday, dealers said.</p>
<p>The Cetes sales were offered or assigned as follows:</p>
<p>    AMOUNT     TERM	 AVERAGE RATE</p>
<p>    150 million    359 days   22.97 pct</p>
<p>    150 million    177 days   22.01 pct</p>
<p>    150 million     86 days   21.69 pct</p>
<p>The terms and maturities of the repurchase agreements were offered as follows:</p>
<p>    500 million     24 days   21.52 pct</p>
<p>    500 million	6 days   21.50 pct</p>
<p>    141 million	1 day    22.00 pct</p>
<p>*Amounts in pesos</p>
<p>(( --Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
</text>
